      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1350379344,
      "text": "Garcinia afzelii is a species of small to medium tree in the family Clusiaceae. It is native to west and west-central tropical Africa, ranging from Guinea to Ghana and from Nigeria to Cameroon, Gabon, Republic of the Congo, and the Central African Republic. It is sometimes called \"bitter kola\", but this name properly refers to G. kola."
    }
